// PLAYTEST: does a Leech's drain pay for the round it costs, or is it a
// worse attack with a garnish?
//
// One of seven files — `player-class-striker`, `-bastion`, `-medic`,
// `-saboteur`, `-leech`, `-invoker`, `-decompiler` — identical in every field but `character`. See
// `player-class-striker.ron` for the shared argument: why the pack is this
// pack, why the pool is unspent, and why **the headless bin reports the same
// numbers for all seven at this level** (it plays All-Attack and invokes
// nothing, so it is the floor rather than the measurement). At level 8 and
// above that stops being true — a Striker's second ordinary swing is
// something the bin does see.
//
//     FERAL_DEV_ARENA=1 cargo run  ->  [R] Arena  ->  [L] player-class-leech
//
// The floor, 2026-09-01, 20 reps, seeds 1-20: 60% won, mean 18.6 rounds,
// 26% player Integrity left, 1.15 companions down. Compare deltas within one
// build only.
//
// Leech Single is `Drain(power: 10, spread: 2, heal_fraction: 0.5)`, so at
// 1.3 it is a small hit that returns half of what actually lands. It is the
// one starter that does two jobs in one round, and the one most likely to be
// strictly worse than both — a drain that heals off damage *dealt* returns
// less against an armoured target, and this pack's mitigation is what
// decides whether it pays.
//
// What to watch:
//   - Against a full-Integrity you, the heal half is wasted. Against a
//     nearly-dead you it may be the round that saves the run. Does the
//     routine have a moment, or is it always the wrong choice?
//   - Compare it directly to Fork Bomb Single (`stack_smash`, 9 authored
//     power against this 10) on a Striker at the same 1.3: the drain costs
//     one more Power and hits for about the same, so the entire difference
//     is the half it gives back.
//   - Leech damps Buff at 0.8, and this kit has no buff, so the trade is
//     invisible here by construction. Fight `player-class-bastion.ron` and
//     then this one with `hyperthread` picked on the wizard to see it.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 5, zone: 1),
    character: (
        class: Some(Leech),
        stats: (0, 0, 0, 0),
        routine: Some("siphon_cycles"),
    ),
    party: [
        (species: "glitch", level: 5),
        (species: "glitch", level: 5),
    ],
    opponents: [
        (species: "sub_process", count: 5),
        (species: "sub_process", count: 5),
    ],
    reps: 1,
    seed: 2,
)
